bring is.tung

## `a` is grounded under `smaller` when every `y smaller a` is
## grounded. selfcalling on a groundedness seething is structural, so a
## fall may selfcall on any input that a wellgrounded relation maketh
## smaller.
show ilk grounded: [α: *, smaller: [α, α, *], α, *] {
  ground: [@a: α, [y: α, y smaller a, α grounded smaller y], α grounded smaller a]
}

## a relation is wellgrounded when every worth is grounded.
show let wellgrounded: [α: *, smaller: [α, α, *], *] ≔ [a: α, α grounded smaller a]

## selfcalling on a groundedness seething. `step` defineth the outcome at `x`
## from the outcomes at every smaller worth.
show let selfcall: [@α: *, @smaller: [α, α, *], @drive: [α, *],
  step: [a: α, [b: α, b smaller a, b drive], a drive],
  a: α, smaller_grounded ground: α grounded smaller a, a drive] ≔
  a step {b, below ^ step selfcall b (b smaller_grounded below)}

## selfcalling on every worth of a wellgrounded relation.
show let wellgrounded_selfcall: [@α: *, @smaller: [α, α, *], @drive: [α, *],
  founded: α wellgrounded smaller,
  step: [a: α, [b: α, b smaller a, b drive], a drive],
  a: α, a drive] ≔
  step selfcall a (a founded)

## wellgrounded selfcalling with an explicit outcome drive.
show let wellgrounded_selfcall_toward: [@α: *, @smaller: [α, α, *],
  drive: [α, *],
  founded: α wellgrounded smaller,
  step: [a: α, [b: α, b smaller a, b drive], a drive],
  a: α, a drive] ≔
  founded wellgrounded_selfcall step a

## selfcall on any input whose mete is smaller. the outcome may hang on
## the input. only the mete needeth a wellgrounded relation.
show let wellgrounded_selfcall_by: [@α: *, @μ: *, @smaller: [μ, μ, *],
  drive: [α, *], mete: [α, μ], founded: μ wellgrounded smaller,
  step: [a: α, [b: α, (b mete) smaller (a mete), b drive], a drive],
  a: α, a drive] ≔
## each meted worth carrieth the original input and its equation.
  ({at ^ [x: α, (x mete) = at, x drive]}) wellgrounded_selfcall_toward founded
    {at, selfcaller, x, same ^ x step {b, below ^
      (b mete) selfcaller (match same { eftbend ^ below }) b eftbend
    }}
  (a mete) a eftbend
